  "result": "Both methods now follow ECMA-402 when `agent.intl` is on, and keep the ECMA-262 behaviour when it's off. The ticket's test262 run (`intl402/String/prototype/toLocaleUpperCase/` and `toLocaleLowerCase/`) passes 18 of 18, and `cargo clippy` is clean. I didn't run the rest of test262, so I haven't checked the `agent.intl`-off path against it.\n\nTransformCase lives in `prototype_to_locale_upper_case.rs` and the lower-case file reuses it. It maps case with ICU4X's `CaseMapper` and treats `az`, `el`, `lt` and `tr` as the locales with language-specific case mappings. Any other requested locale resolves to `und`. I picked that locale list myself, since the spec leaves it to the implementation.\n\nLone surrogates have no case mapping, so each one is copied through unchanged and splits the string into separately mapped runs.",
